course: dictionary
lesson: 1409
title: Long words, broken into parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some long words are built from smaller parts that you may already know. Break the word into pieces, and each piece can give you a clue. Cardiopulmonary is built from cardio, which means heart, and pulmonary, which means lungs.
explain: Put the parts together and you get "heart and lungs together". Cardiopulmonary is an adjective, so it describes something. It tells you that the heart and the lungs are working as a team.
explain: You will mostly meet this word in first aid lessons, in the short form CPR. «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest to keep blood moving when the heart has stopped, and the call handler can talk anyone through it.» The words around it show that CPR is about helping someone whose heart has stopped.
fact: Cardio means heart.
fact: Pulmonary means lungs.
fact: Cardiopulmonary means to do with both the heart and the lungs together.
fact: «Cardiopulmonary resuscitation» is the full name of CPR.
fact: The lungs pick up oxygen, and the heart pumps the blood round the body. When they work together, blood keeps moving.
exercise: What does cardio mean? | Brain | *Heart | Lungs | Blood
exercise: «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means pressing hard and fast on the middle of the chest.» Which part of the body is pressed? | *The middle of the chest | The back of the head | The arm | The knee
exercise: Which word means to do with both the heart and the lungs together? | Pulmonary | Cardio | *Cardiopulmonary | Resuscitation
test: A doctor says the cardiopulmonary system is working well. What is working well? | The eyes and ears | Only the legs | *The heart and the lungs together | The bones alone
test: From «CPR, cardiopulmonary resuscitation, means...», what is the main job of CPR? | Calming someone down with a joke | Cleaning a cut | Making the heart beat slower | *Keeping blood moving when the heart has stopped
exam: Which two parts make up cardiopulmonary, and what does each mean? | Both parts mean the chest | Cardio means lungs and pulmonary means heart | *Cardio means heart and pulmonary means lungs | Cardio means blood and pulmonary means skin
